colour=0xffcd05

[com_25]
type=graphic
x=8
y=35
width=35
height=35
layer=com_4
graphic="bank_buttons_new1,2"
colour=0xffffffff
transmitop=1,10
op1=Swap/insert
op10= 

[com_26]
type=graphic
x=11
y=12
width=35
height=35
layer=com_5
graphic="bank_buttons_new1,4"
colour=0xffffffff
transmitop=1,10
op1=Item/note withdrawal
op10= 

[com_27]
type=text
x=56
y=15
width=391
height=79
layer=com_5
textfont=p11_full
fontmono=no
text=Item/note withdrawal: Clicking this button toggles how you withdraw items from your bank. `Item' mode places the actual item in your inventory; `Note' mode places a `noted' version of that object in your inventory. A note is worth the exact same value as the item it depicts, but is not the item itself and cannot be used as such. Notes are typically used for trading in bulk, as noted items can be stacked even if the actual item cannot be.
textlineheight=12
textshadow=yes
transmitop=10
op10= 

[com_28]
type=text
x=56
y=111
width=391
height=79
layer=com_5
textfont=p11_full
fontmono=no
text=Deposit carried items and worn items. One button empties all of the items from your inventory, while the other moves all of the items you are wearing into your bank, if there is space. Items that cannot be placed in your bank will stay where they are.    
textlineheight=12
textshadow=yes
transmitop=10
op10=  

[com_29]
type=graphic
x=11
y=106
width=35
height=35
layer=com_5
graphic="bank_buttons_new2,0"
colour=0xffffffff
transmitop=1,10
op1=Deposit carried items
op10=   

[com_30]
type=graphic
x=14
y=114
width=29
height=21
layer=com_5
graphic="bank_bob_button,1"
colour=0xffffffff
transmitop=10
op10=    

[com_31]
type=graphic
x=11
y=140
width=35
height=35
layer=com_5
graphic="bank_buttons_new2,0"
colour=0xffffffff
transmitop=1,10
op1=Deposit worn items
op10=    

[com_32]
type=graphic
x=14
y=148
width=29
height=21
layer=com_5
graphic="bank_bob_button,2"
colour=0xffffffff
transmitop=10
op10=    

[com_33]
type=text
x=8
y=3
width=436
height=33
layer=com_4
textfont=p11_full
fontmono=no
text=Across the bottom of the bank there are some other features, which, from left to right, are: 
textlineheight=12
textshadow=yes
transmitop=10
op10= 

[com_34]
type=text
x=53
y=39
width=391
height=79
layer=com_4
textfont=p11_full
fontmono=no
text=Swap/insert: Clicking this button toggles how items are rearranged in your bank. `Swap' mode means that the item you drag and the item it is dragged over will swap places in your bank. `Insert' mode allows you to place an item in a specific bank slot, shifting other items over to make room.
textlineheight=12
textshadow=yes
transmitop=10
op10= 

[com_35]
type=text
x=53
y=117
width=391
height=79
layer=com_4
textfont=p11_full
fontmono=no
text=Search: Clicking this button will switch your bank to the main tab and open a search box. Type the name of the item you are looking for and it will narrow down your banked items as you type. (Note: don't worry, your other items aren't disappearing, they're just being removed from the current search and are still in your bank.) 
textlineheight=12
textshadow=yes
transmitop=10
op10= 

[com_36]
type=graphic
x=8
y=113
width=35
height=35
layer=com_4
graphic="bank_buttons_new2,0"

[com_37]
type=graphic
x=8
y=113
width=35
height=35
layer=com_4
graphic="bank_buttons_new1,0"
colour=0xffffffff
transmitop=1,10
op1=Search
op10=  
opcursor0=cursor_56

[com_38]
type=text
x=8
y=5
width=436
height=43
layer=com_2
textfont=p11_full
fontmono=no
text=The Bank of RuneScape is a great place to keep all of your belongings safe. The bank has branches all over RuneScape, so you're never very far away from your possessions.
textlineheight=12
textshadow=yes

[com_39]
type=text
x=71
y=64
width=371
height=58
layer=com_2
textfont=p11_full
fontmono=no
text=The tab furthest to the left is the main bank tab (pictured left). The main tab will always display the entire contents of your bank account, but you can also create up to eight other tabs in which to categorise your banked items.
textlineheight=12
textshadow=yes

[com_40]
type=text
x=16
y=132
width=371
height=76
layer=com_2
textfont=p11_full
fontmono=no
text=To create a new tab, simply drag any item in your bank on to the `plus' tab (pictured right). You can then drag as many other items as you want on to this new tab. Clicking on a tab other than the main one will show you only those items you have placed within it. The icon used to mark each new tab is taken from the first item within that tab.
textlineheight=12
textshadow=yes

[com_41]
type=graphic
x=12
y=57
width=48
height=48
layer=com_2
graphic="bank_tabs,1"
colour=0xffffffff

[com_42]
type=graphic
x=19
y=71
width=36
height=32
layer=com_2
graphic="bank_misc_graphics,0"
colour=0xffffffff

[com_43]
type=graphic
x=394
y=129
width=48
height=48
layer=com_2
graphic="bank_tabs,1"
colour=0xffffffff

[com_44]
type=graphic
x=401
y=143
width=36
height=32
layer=com_2
graphic="bank_misc_graphics,1"
colour=0xffffffff

[com_45]
type=text
x=12
y=5
width=436
height=82
layer=com_3
textfont=p11_full
fontmono=no
text=Using this tab system will allow you to easily group together related items as you wish. For instance, you could place all of your food in one tab, or all of your weapons in another. Alternatively, you could create a tab to contain all of those items you use to train a skill or play a certain activity. There is no limit to the number of times you can rearrange your bank, so feel free to experiment. 
textlineheight=12
textshadow=yes

[com_46]
type=text
x=3
y=96
width=293
height=29
xmode=abs_right
layer=com_3
textfont=p11_full
fontmono=no
text=Near the bottom-left corner of the bank you will see a set of four numbers, as shown to the left.
textlineheight=12
textshadow=yes

[com_47]
type=layer
x=38
y=97
width=90
height=25
layer=com_3
transmitop=10
op10=  

[com_48]
type=text
x=12
y=137
width=436
height=66
layer=com_3
textfont=p11_full
fontmono=no
text=The first two numbers, separated by a diagonal line, represent your non-member bank space and how much of that bank space you have filled with non-member items. The second two numbers, separated by the other diagonal line, represent the bank space you have gained by being a member, and how much of that bank space you have filled with member items.
textlineheight=12
textshadow=yes
transmitop=10
op10= 

